this case, we have that  \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x=151.3-0.7x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that all assumptions for a simple regression model are held. So, given a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the slope ${\\beta }_{1}$ of our model can be written as\n\n$$\n{\\beta }_{0}\\,\\pm \\,\\overset{\\text{margin of error}}{\\overset{⏞}{{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]}}.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $\\,{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}$ is our point estimate for the intercept, computed using the data points from our sample.\n\n- $P(T>{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-2$ degrees of freedom.\n\n- $\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]$ is the standard error of ${\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\text{MSE}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{{\\overset{―}{x}}^{2}}{{S}_{xx}})}\n$$\n\nwhere we have:\n\n- $\\text{MSE}$ is the mean squared error of the model:\n\n$$\n\\text{MSE}=\\frac{1}{n-2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-{\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i})^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i}$ is the estimate of ${y}_{i}$ given by our regression model.\n\n- ${S}_{xx}$ is the usual sum of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\n$$\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate. From the regression equation $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=151.3-0.7x,$ our point estimate is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}=151.3.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. \n\n- Since we are interested in finding a $98%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.98=0.02\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.01.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>6.965)=0.01.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}={t}_{2,0.01}=6.965.\n$$\n\n- Computing ${S}_{xx},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} & =(60-64)^{2}+(62-64)^{2}+(66-64)^{2}+(68-64)^{2} \\\\  & =16+4+4+16 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=6.965\\cdot \\sqrt{7.7\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{{64}^{2}}{40})}≈195.8\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Determine the limits of the confidence interval:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,\\pm \\,{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=151.3\\pm 195.8\n$$"] ["question-a77fcdca-ce6d-5371-a7a2-e886bf8d2462" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5"] ["answer-e489115e-e8c1-5d14-a654-2c4be9ba3e26" :answer/id #uuid "e489115e-e8c1-5d14-a654-2c4be9ba3e26"] ["answer-e489115e-e8c1-5d14-a654-2c4be9ba3e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e489115e-e8c1-5d14-a654-2c4be9ba3e26" :answer/value "151.3\\pm 173.1"] ["answer-ac8ab9d8-4875-5fd3-8eff-2b8511dc815e" :answer/id #uuid "ac8ab9d8-4875-5fd3-8eff-2b8511dc815e"] ["answer-ac8ab9d8-4875-5fd3-8eff-2b8511dc815e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ac8ab9d8-4875-5fd3-8eff-2b8511dc815e" :answer/value "151.3\\pm 175.2"] ["answer-4b209ccf-fac3-51cd-a24e-17d94342e720" :answer/id #uuid "4b209ccf-fac3-51cd-a24e-17d94342e720"] ["answer-4b209ccf-fac3-51cd-a24e-17d94342e720" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4b209ccf-fac3-51cd-a24e-17d94342e720" :answer/value "151.3\\pm 183.6"] ["answer-7e50f150-1d03-5cdd-b228-0b83996b3433" :answer/id #uuid "7e50f150-1d03-5cdd-b228-0b83996b3433"] ["answer-7e50f150-1d03-5cdd-b228-0b83996b3433" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7e50f150-1d03-5cdd-b228-0b83996b3433" :answer/value "151.3\\pm 193.8"] ["answer-9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0" :answer/id #uuid "9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0"] ["answer-9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0" :answer/value "151.3\\pm 195.8"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/correct "answer-9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/choices "answer-e489115e-e8c1-5d14-a654-2c4be9ba3e26"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/choices "answer-ac8ab9d8-4875-5fd3-8eff-2b8511dc815e"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/choices "answer-4b209ccf-fac3-51cd-a24e-17d94342e720"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/choices "answer-7e50f150-1d03-5cdd-b228-0b83996b3433"] ["answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5" :answer-field/choices "answer-9f303830-c78a-5b75-886c-4c70713deba0"] ["question-a77fcdca-ce6d-5371-a7a2-e886bf8d2462" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b2fd0291-b761-5650-8e97-a72f4f5d21b5"] [17592186192683 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a77fcdca-ce6d-5371-a7a2-e886bf8d2462"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/id #uuid "4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-159556"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/problem "| **Age ($x$)** | **$34$** | **$36$** | **$40$** | **$42$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Hours of sleep ($y$)** | $6.5$ | $7$ | $7.5$ | $8$ |\n\nThe table above shows the ages, in years, and the number of hours each of four randomly selected adults slept last night. The corresponding linear regression line fitted using this sample is $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=0.6+0.2x.$\nAssuming that all conditions for the simple regression model are satisfied, $\\overset{―}{x}=38,$ and $\\text{MSE}=0.0125,$ find an $80%$ confidence interval for the $y$-intercept of the regression line. \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>1.886)=0.1,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $2$ degrees of freedom. Also, the standard error for the $y$-intecept is* \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\text{MSE}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{{\\overset{―}{x}}^{2}}{{S}_{xx}})}.\n$$"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/worked-solution "We use the following notations:\n\n- $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ is the regression line that best fits the population, and\n\n- $\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x$ is the estimate of the \"true\" regression line given by the data in our sample.\n\nIn this case, we have that  \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x=0.6+0.2x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that all assumptions for a simple regression model are held. So, given a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the slope ${\\beta }_{1}$ of our model can be written as\n\n$$\n{\\beta }_{0}\\,\\pm \\,\\overset{\\text{margin of error}}{\\overset{⏞}{{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]}}.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $\\,{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}$ is our point estimate for the intercept, computed using the data points from our sample.\n\n- $P(T>{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-2$ degrees of freedom.\n\n- $\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]$ is the standard error of ${\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\text{MSE}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{{\\overset{―}{x}}^{2}}{{S}_{xx}})}\n$$\n\nwhere we have:\n\n- $\\text{MSE}$ is the mean squared error of the model:\n\n$$\n\\text{MSE}=\\frac{1}{n-2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-{\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i})^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i}$ is the estimate of ${y}_{i}$ given by our regression model.\n\n- ${S}_{xx}$ is the usual sum of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\n$$\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate. From the regression equation $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=0.6+0.2x,$ our point estimate is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}=0.6.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. \n\n- Since we are interested in finding a $80%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.8=0.2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.1.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>1.886)=0.1.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}={t}_{2,0.1}=1.886.\n$$\n\n- Computing ${S}_{xx},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} & =(34-38)^{2}+(36-38)^{2}+(40-38)^{2}+(42-38)^{2} \\\\  & =16+4+4+16 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=1.886\\cdot \\sqrt{0.0125\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{{38}^{2}}{40})}≈1.3\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Determine the limits of the confidence interval:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,\\pm \\,{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}\\,]=0.6\\pm 1.3\n$$"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/id #uuid "67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178"] ["answer-b3c741e7-dfd7-5769-bd67-c9d073965e46" :answer/id #uuid "b3c741e7-dfd7-5769-bd67-c9d073965e46"] ["answer-b3c741e7-dfd7-5769-bd67-c9d073965e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b3c741e7-dfd7-5769-bd67-c9d073965e46" :answer/value "0.6\\pm 0.2"] ["answer-6fb2e354-67fd-5920-b3f1-8def0deb29e2" :answer/id #uuid "6fb2e354-67fd-5920-b3f1-8def0deb29e2"] ["answer-6fb2e354-67fd-5920-b3f1-8def0deb29e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6fb2e354-67fd-5920-b3f1-8def0deb29e2" :answer/value "0.6\\pm 1.1"] ["answer-94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a" :answer/id #uuid "94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a"] ["answer-94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a" :answer/value "0.6\\pm 1.3"] ["answer-62649176-19b3-5dc9-882a-69ef22eb63b6" :answer/id #uuid "62649176-19b3-5dc9-882a-69ef22eb63b6"] ["answer-62649176-19b3-5dc9-882a-69ef22eb63b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-62649176-19b3-5dc9-882a-69ef22eb63b6" :answer/value "0.6\\pm 1.5"] ["answer-7ec24db7-f765-5318-ae89-7d5a90748c37" :answer/id #uuid "7ec24db7-f765-5318-ae89-7d5a90748c37"] ["answer-7ec24db7-f765-5318-ae89-7d5a90748c37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7ec24db7-f765-5318-ae89-7d5a90748c37" :answer/value "0.6\\pm 1.8"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/correct "answer-94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/choices "answer-b3c741e7-dfd7-5769-bd67-c9d073965e46"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/choices "answer-6fb2e354-67fd-5920-b3f1-8def0deb29e2"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/choices "answer-94f6c867-15bb-5d02-aa0b-4ba6976af87a"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/choices "answer-62649176-19b3-5dc9-882a-69ef22eb63b6"] ["answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178" :answer-field/choices "answer-7ec24db7-f765-5318-ae89-7d5a90748c37"] ["question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-67039e40-5de3-570b-bbed-0d3b0e5de178"] [17592186192683 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4f56dfe4-956b-5759-bcb7-ccce82fe1dbd"] ["question-8c255cc5-a4ec-5d1f-be58-dbb45c0a4d57" :question/id #uuid "8c25